.git
.codegraph
.worktrees
target/*
!target/identify-release
!target/identify-release/**
!target/identify-data
!target/identify-data/**
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vitest-attachments
**/__screenshots__
# The built identify tree is generated, never a build input: both images build
# it inside the image or copy it from `target/` with `IDENTIFY_DATA=prebuilt`.
# Left in, a pack change would invalidate the `COPY . .` layer and the whole
# wasm compile behind it.
crates/rom-weaver-cli/data/identify/v1/*
prototype
third_party
*.log

# Not build inputs. These change often (CI, most docs, and browser-test
# commits), and anything left here invalidates the `COPY . .` layer and with it
# the whole wasm+cargo build. Published Markdown is an exception: Vite renders
# it into the webapp. Root *.md stays: several are read at build time
# (README as the workspace `readme`, CHANGELOG by the webapp version script's
# fallbacks).
#
# This is the only ignore file either image gets. Both builds use the repo root
# as context, and BuildKit reads `<context>/.dockerignore` or a sibling
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` - never a `.dockerignore` that merely lives beside
# the image's other sources.
.github
# The webapp build reads every published guide, so these are build inputs. Kept
# per shelf rather than per file: a new guide is published by adding it to its
# folder, and listing files here would be a second place to forget. The hub and
# the FAQ sit at the top of `docs/`, so they are named individually.
docs/*
!docs/README.md
!docs/faq.md
!docs/tutorials
!docs/tutorials/**
!docs/how-to
!docs/how-to/**
!docs/explanation
!docs/explanation/**
!docs/hosting
!docs/hosting/**
!docs/reference
!docs/reference/**
!docs/development
!docs/development/**
!docs/screenshots
!docs/screenshots/**
!docs/legal
!docs/legal/**
# The release image copies the generated man pages and completions from here
# (`docs-prebuilt` in the Dockerfile) after docker-publish.yml extracts them.
!docs/man
!docs/man/**
!docs/completions
!docs/completions/**
packages/rom-weaver-webapp/tests
